{
  "topic": "odd-one-numbers",
  "source": "KSQAAC Spardha Yashassu NMMS Study Material 2022, MAT Chapter 18 (questions: PDF page 61, solutions: PDF pages 139–142)",
  "questions": [
    {
      "id": "oo-b01", "bookNo": 1, "sourcePage": 61, "keyFrom": "book", "pattern": "odd-one", "layout": "odd",
      "terms": ["363", "462", "584", "792"],
      "options": {"A": "363", "B": "462", "C": "584", "D": "792"}, "answer": "C",
      "rule": "In each number the middle digit is the sum of the outer two: 363 → 3 + 3 = 6, 462 → 4 + 2 = 6, 792 → 7 + 2 = 9.",
      "working": "584: 5 + 4 = 9, not 8"
    },
    {
      "id": "oo-b02", "bookNo": 2, "sourcePage": 61, "keyFrom": "book", "pattern": "odd-one", "layout": "odd", "status": "needs-review",
      "terms": ["7", "13", "21", "29"],
      "options": {"A": "7", "B": "13", "C": "21", "D": "29"}, "answer": "D",
      "rule": "The book's rule: n² − n + 1 for n = 3, 4, 5, 6 gives 7, 13, 21, 31.",
      "working": "6² − 6 + 1 = 31, not 29",
      "note": "Hidden until checked: 21 is also an odd one out, as the only number that is not prime (7, 13 and 29 are prime). The question has two defensible answers."
    },
    {
      "id": "oo-b03", "bookNo": 3, "sourcePage": 61, "keyFrom": "book", "pattern": "odd-one", "layout": "odd",
      "terms": ["3782", "4591", "5726", "6950"],
      "options": {"A": "3782", "B": "4591", "C": "5726", "D": "6950"}, "answer": "B",
      "rule": "The digits of each number add up to 20: 3 + 7 + 8 + 2 = 20, 5 + 7 + 2 + 6 = 20, 6 + 9 + 5 + 0 = 20.",
      "working": "4591: 4 + 5 + 9 + 1 = 19, not 20"
    },
    {
      "id": "oo-b04", "bookNo": 4, "sourcePage": 61, "keyFrom": "book", "pattern": "odd-one", "layout": "odd",
      "terms": ["1, 3", "3, 13", "5, 30", "7, 57"],
      "options": {"A": "1, 3", "B": "3, 13", "C": "5, 30", "D": "7, 57"}, "answer": "C",
      "rule": "In each pair the second number is n² + n + 1: 1 → 1 + 1 + 1 = 3, 3 → 9 + 3 + 1 = 13, 7 → 49 + 7 + 1 = 57.",
      "working": "5 → 25 + 5 + 1 = 31, not 30"
    },
    {
      "id": "oo-b05", "bookNo": 5, "sourcePage": 61, "keyFrom": "book", "pattern": "odd-one", "layout": "odd",
      "terms": ["57875", "73573", "86468", "94149"],
      "options": {"A": "57875", "B": "73573", "C": "86468", "D": "94149"}, "answer": "B",
      "rule": "The others are palindromes: they read the same backwards (57875, 86468, 94149).",
      "working": "73573 backwards is 37537, so it is not a palindrome"
    },
    {
      "id": "oo-b06", "bookNo": 6, "sourcePage": 61, "keyFrom": "book", "pattern": "odd-one", "layout": "odd",
      "terms": ["1, 2, 5", "2, 3, 17", "3, 4, 42", "4, 5, 89"],
      "options": {"A": "1, 2, 5", "B": "2, 3, 17", "C": "3, 4, 42", "D": "4, 5, 89"}, "answer": "C",
      "rule": "In each group, (1st)³ + (2nd)² = 3rd: 1³ + 2² = 5, 2³ + 3² = 17, 4³ + 5² = 89.",
      "working": "3³ + 4² = 27 + 16 = 43, not 42"
    },
    {
      "id": "oo-b07", "bookNo": 7, "sourcePage": 61, "keyFrom": "book", "pattern": "odd-one", "layout": "odd",
      "terms": ["17/GA", "29/IB", "73/CG", "54/DF"],
      "options": {"A": "17/GA", "B": "29/IB", "C": "73/CG", "D": "54/DF"}, "answer": "D",
      "rule": "The letters are the digits written in reverse, as places in the alphabet: 17 → G A (7, 1), 29 → I B (9, 2), 73 → C G (3, 7).",
      "working": "54 → D E (4, 5), but the letters are D F"
    },
    {
      "id": "oo-b08", "bookNo": 8, "sourcePage": 61, "keyFrom": "book", "pattern": "odd-one", "layout": "odd",
      "terms": ["50, 168", "52, 142", "54, 126", "58, 184"],
      "options": {"A": "50, 168", "B": "52, 142", "C": "54, 126", "D": "58, 184"}, "answer": "A",
      "rule": "The digits of both numbers add up to the same total: 52 and 142 → 7, 54 and 126 → 9, 58 and 184 → 13.",
      "working": "50 → 5 + 0 = 5, but 168 → 1 + 6 + 8 = 15"
    },
    {
      "id": "oo-b09", "bookNo": 9, "sourcePage": 61, "keyFrom": "book", "pattern": "odd-one", "layout": "odd",
      "terms": ["324, 24", "123, 6", "314, 14", "706, 0"],
      "options": {"A": "324, 24", "B": "123, 6", "C": "314, 14", "D": "706, 0"}, "answer": "C",
      "rule": "The second number is the product of the digits of the first: 324 → 3 × 2 × 4 = 24, 123 → 1 × 2 × 3 = 6, 706 → 7 × 0 × 6 = 0.",
      "working": "314 → 3 × 1 × 4 = 12, not 14"
    },
    {
      "id": "oo-b10", "bookNo": 10, "sourcePage": 61, "keyFrom": "book", "pattern": "odd-one", "layout": "odd",
      "terms": ["542", "725", "761", "835"],
      "options": {"A": "542", "B": "725", "C": "761", "D": "835"}, "answer": "A",
      "rule": "1st digit − 2nd digit = 3rd digit: 725 → 7 − 2 = 5, 761 → 7 − 6 = 1, 835 → 8 − 3 = 5.",
      "working": "542: 5 − 4 = 1, not 2"
    },
    {
      "id": "oo-b11", "bookNo": 11, "sourcePage": 61, "keyFrom": "book", "pattern": "odd-one", "layout": "odd",
      "terms": ["124", "215", "342", "513"],
      "options": {"A": "124", "B": "215", "C": "342", "D": "513"}, "answer": "D",
      "rule": "The others are one less than a cube: 124 = 5³ − 1, 215 = 6³ − 1, 342 = 7³ − 1.",
      "working": "513 = 8³ + 1, one more than a cube"
    },
    {
      "id": "oo-b12", "bookNo": 12, "sourcePage": 61, "keyFrom": "book", "pattern": "odd-one", "layout": "odd",
      "terms": ["11/14", "13/23", "17/31", "19/45"],
      "options": {"A": "11/14", "B": "13/23", "C": "17/31", "D": "19/45"}, "answer": "C",
      "rule": "Numerator + denominator is a square number: 11 + 14 = 25 = 5², 13 + 23 = 36 = 6², 19 + 45 = 64 = 8².",
      "working": "17 + 31 = 48, which is not a square number"
    },
    {
      "id": "oo-b13", "bookNo": 13, "sourcePage": 61, "keyFrom": "book", "pattern": "odd-one", "layout": "odd",
      "terms": ["111", "263", "383", "482"],
      "options": {"A": "111", "B": "263", "C": "383", "D": "482"}, "answer": "C",
      "rule": "1st digit × 3rd digit = middle digit: 111 → 1 × 1 = 1, 263 → 2 × 3 = 6, 482 → 4 × 2 = 8.",
      "working": "383: 3 × 3 = 9, not 8"
    },
    {
      "id": "oo-b14", "bookNo": 14, "sourcePage": 61, "keyFrom": "book", "pattern": "odd-one", "layout": "odd",
      "terms": ["27", "37", "47", "97"],
      "options": {"A": "27", "B": "37", "C": "47", "D": "97"}, "answer": "A",
      "rule": "37, 47 and 97 are prime numbers.",
      "working": "27 = 3 × 9, so it is not a prime number"
    },
    {
      "id": "oo-b15", "bookNo": 15, "sourcePage": 61, "keyFrom": "book", "pattern": "odd-one", "layout": "odd",
